{"agent_id":"pp3g-XX0J-validation-evidence-only-task-no-system-to-ship-test","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T06:16:54.884229958Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b22a89ff-e016-4eab-9282-4e69d8ca729f","comment_uuid":"8a1024b2-caa5-4103-b3ec-8eebf4987867","author":"pp3g-XX0J-validation-evidence-only-task-no-system-to-ship-test","content":"Result: retry-classification validation complete — classification alone ELIMINATES the compounding (4x -> 1x spawns), with one residual gap (caller-visible error shape + C2 variant).\n\nCommit ff25820 (18 files, research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/retry-classification/): proxy_classified.py (single-variable delta on #213 drift proxy), backend.py + manifest.json (byte-identical copies, md5-verified), tests/ (phase_1_control, phase_2_classified, phase_3_connection, phase_3b_proxy_retry, common_retry, run_retry), logs/ per test, report.md.\n\nKEY NUMBERS (toolregistry==0.15.0, mcp==2.0.0, py3.10.12; host load avg ~15/4 cores inflated absolutes, per-run init_ms logged):\n- Test 1 CONTROL (unmodified drift proxy): 4 backend spawns, 2 persistent proxies (+1 registration), reconnect_fired=True, 12176-42518 ms (n=4) — 4x multiplier still reproduces exactly.\n- Test 2 CLASSIFIED: 1 backend spawn, 1 persistent proxy, reconnect_fired=False (NO fresh proxy_started after failure), 4224-14471 ms (n=5); matched-run ratio T2/T1 = 0.25-0.43. Error text preserved VERBATIM (full jsonschema detail inside the caller-visible result).\n- Test 3 (kill proxy mid-call): reconnect STILL fires (3 proxies), retried call succeeds 5.0.\n- Test 3B (kill backend mid-call, supplementary): proxy's OWN respawn-retry STILL fires (MCPError(-32000 Connection closed) -> respawn -> retry_succeeded), no misclassification.\n\nVERDICT: YES — classification alone removes the compounding: spawns 4->1 (75% reduction), proxies 2->1, latency 57-75% lower (matched-run ratio). Residual single-failure cost = one spawn + forward + classify (~4.2-14.5 s here, dominated by the single backend init; ~1.35-2.2x the #213 success baseline). Residual gap: (1) caller-visible shape degrades from ErrorResult to ToolCallResult-with-repr (ToolRegistry 0.15.0 only builds ErrorResult from a raised exception — the exact path that fires connection.py:106 — so proxy-only classification cannot have both no-reconnect AND ErrorResult); (2) the consistently-drifted C2 variant (backend declaration+behaviour both diverged) is invisible to proxy-side classification (2 spawns/2 proxies remain). Heavier mitigation would need to save only the single-spawn residual + fix the error shape + reach C2. Report: research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/retry-classification/report.md","created_at":"2026-08-06T06:16:54.869681845Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:FZhKCZXb2m48Kkv4hiOg7SGI5tHHFv5+sYldGFVanHU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg++yESydc6rh4C1AeKGWti3YO+o09CRHO3M+PRxshLasAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAOQkP56PJlcIp07B/goJyA8fGyQp/1w4k/4E0KcyC9QdYQjqouTRGUn+vZH5XSly2uLgZg6/8mwnSakJKfuwcDQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:FZhKCZXb2m48Kkv4hiOg7SGI5tHHFv5+sYldGFVanHU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg++yESydc6rh4C1AeKGWti3YO+o09CRHO3M+PRxshLasAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHQlQGyN9GfiARqAK1GX+IFrwAZBZfy29C4yYMLTGq03mJHRvg1tSL3cjs1MiJS3rpkXF7ejnSuB7nUJJFwijAA="}
